2.  If the diners are required to take care of the disposal themselves, staff should remind them in a timely manner to clean up and dispose of the excrement properly, and may consider providing relevant tools (such as gloves, plastic bags and sanitisers) to assist them. If a diner refuses or fails to do so promptly, staff must be deployed to look after the matter as soon as possible.
